  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The part is $24,$ the percentage is $30%,$ and we need to find the whole.\n\nTo do this, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{whole}=\\text{part}÷\\text{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $30%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{30}{100}=\\frac{30÷10}{100÷10}=\\frac{3}{10}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =24÷30% \\\\  & =24÷\\frac{3}{10} \\\\  & =24\\times \\frac{10}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{3}\\times 10 \\\\  & =8\\times 10 \\\\  & =80\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $80\\times 30%=24.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
